#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161689 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162123 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9040153-b66c-5c55-8854-8c5be0309720" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Expected Value Given a Conditional Mass Function"}] :question/id #uuid "07199b8b-32c6-59f5-b452-da48648cb799" :question/math-academy-id "e-10298" :question/problem "| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_{Y|X}(y \\,|\\, 2)$ | $\\dfrac{2}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ |\n\nFind the $\\textrm{E}\\big[Y \\,|\\, X=2\\big]$ given that the conditional probability mass function $f_{Y|X}(y \\,|\\, 2)$ is shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "The conditional expected value of  $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\big[Y \\,|\\, X=x\\big] = \\sum_{y} y \\, f_{Y | X}(y \\,|\\, x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=2] & ={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,2) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161692 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162126 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "59bd2280-5028-5261-a9ed-61d01d80c29a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Expectation Using Row Totals"}] :question/id #uuid "2f074ddb-056a-51c6-b307-74df33f135f0" :question/math-academy-id "e-10305" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{8}{27}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{27}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\dfrac{2}{27}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ |\n\nFind $\\textrm{E}\\big[Y \\,|\\, X=2\\big]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\big[Y \\,|\\, X=x\\big] = \\sum_{y} y \\, f_{Y | X}(y \\,|\\, x).\n$$\n\nIn order to find $f_{Y | X}(y \\,|\\, x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $f_X(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{8}{27}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{27}$ | $\\dfrac{13}{27}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\dfrac{2}{27}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{27}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\nf_{Y | X}(y \\,|\\, x)  = \\dfrac{f(x,y)}{f_X(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x{:}$\n\n| $f_{Y | X}(y \\,|\\, x)$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{3}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{8}{13}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{13}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\dfrac{2}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{3}{5}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=2] & ={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,2) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{8}{13}+2\\cdot \\frac{5}{13} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161699 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162133 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e47d5ac-cb51-5259-ba41-6c407a992271" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Expectation Using Column Totals"}] :question/id #uuid "4de21bb7-7f18-56c4-9925-47459df6f049" :question/math-academy-id "e-10350" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ |\n\nFind $\\textrm{E}\\big[X \\,|\\, Y=1\\big]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\big[X \\,|\\, Y=y\\big] = \\sum_{x} x \\, f_{X | Y}(x \\,|\\, y).\n$$\n\nIn order to find $f_{X | Y}(x \\,|\\, y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ |\n| $f_Y(y)$ | $\\dfrac{5}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{4}{9}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\nf_{X | Y}(x \\,|\\, y)  = \\dfrac{f(x,y)}{f_Y(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y{:}$\n\n| $f_{X | Y}(x \\,|\\, y)$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\dfrac{3}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=1] & ={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}+4\\cdot \\frac{3}{5}+6\\cdot \\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{5} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430547 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162123 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9040153-b66c-5c55-8854-8c5be0309720" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Expected Value Given a Conditional Mass Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04d3bd28-c2f2-5491-924f-6e0c82e09fc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430457} {:answer/id #uuid "154651d3-01b5-5743-b141-561396010474" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430461} {:answer/id #uuid "42dcc74d-758e-5042-9242-b5eb9bfe4e31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430481} {:answer/id #uu